    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27k2BmYGwAVfyK9EzxnR8PX)_\n\n## What changes\n- New module `sp-bibtex-types` (`libraries/modules/academic/`, doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-bibtex-types.org`): one option, `sp-bibtex-types-tag-alist`, from BibTeX entry type to org tag (case-insensitive), plus `sp-bibtex-types-default-tag` (`text`).\n  - booksection → `booksection`, incollection → `incollection`, article → `journalarticle`, book → `book`\n  - collection and mvcollection → `collection`\n  - phdthesis → `phdthesis`, mastersthesis → `mastersthesis`\n  - anything else → `text` (the `base-text` scheme)\n  - Functions: `sp-bibtex-types-tag`, `-entry-tag`, `-all-tags`, `-collection-p`.\n- `sp-litnotes-meta-create-note` (used by `sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-children`) now tags the new note with `litnote` plus the type tag.\n- Reuse in `sp-litnotes-meta--table-view`: the `collection-articles` view is chosen by `sp-bibtex-types-collection-p` instead of its own type list. Behaviour change: `proceedings`/`mvproceedings` now file as `text`, so they get `book-sections`.\n- Schema and tag checks:\n  - `sp-vulpea-schemas` had no schemas for `book`, `phdthesis`, `mastersthesis`; added (each includes `base-text`).\n  - `sp-org-tag-registry`: added `phdthesis`, `mastersthesis` to the literature group.\n  - `sp-litnotes-refs` (tag → BibTeX type for stubs): added `mastersthesis`. It stays a separate table, as the reverse direction is not one-to-one.\n- Docs updated as bullet lists (`sp-bibtex-types.org`, `sp-litnotes-meta.org`, `sp-vulpea.org`, `sp-org-lint.org`, README module table). No CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## Tested\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: new `tests/sp-bibtex-types-test.el` (mapping, default, entry, collection-p, every tag has a schema and a registry entry) and `sp-litnotes-meta-test.el`; 23/23 pass, Vulpea stubbed.\n\n## Not tested\n- Not run on the real vault. The `citar-create-note` path (`sp-litnotes-meta-fill`) does not add a type tag yet; only the backfill does.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDGrRqGutQfyF952mz)_",
